-- CK-59: a record literal met by a `number` expectation is constrained
-- before the meeting fails on the kind, so the message shows the literal's
-- own field types (checker-v2.md §6.5 *Amended by R5*; R5's structural
-- review, S1). On checker v1 at 2bc9e22 it shows `{ a : a, b : b }`.
pub f x =
    Basics.add x { a = 1, b = "s" }
